---
import LegalPage from "../../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { keepAfterStopPaying, operator, paymentProvider } from "../../content/legal";
import { portalLoginUrl, portalWords } from "../../content/billing-login";
const portalUrl = portalLoginUrl();
---

<LegalPage
  title="Refunds"
  description="How refunds for DMbot work, and how to ask for one."
  heading="Refunds"
  summary={[
    "You can stop your plan any time. It keeps working until the end of the period you already paid for.",
    "If we charged you by mistake, or twice, we give the money back.",
    "Extra hours can't be refunded. For anything else, ask us and we'll look at it fairly.",
    "Refunds go back to the card or account you paid with.",
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="stopping">Stopping your plan</h2>
  <p>
    Stop your plan any time from <a href="/account">My Account</a>. You won't be charged again.
    Your plan keeps working until the end of the period you already paid for. After that, your campaigns
    are kept for {keepAfterStopPaying} in case you come back.
  </p>
  {
    portalUrl && (
      <p>
        {portalWords.refunds} <a href={portalUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">{portalWords.linkText}</a>
      </p>
    )
  }
  <p>
    Deleting your account is not the same as stopping your plan: DMbot stops for you at once, you
    won't be charged again, and the rest of the month you paid for isn't paid back. If you want
    money back, write to us before you delete your account (see <a href="#how-to-ask">How to ask</a>).
  </p>

  <h2>When you can get money back</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>A plan you just started and haven't used:</strong> write to {operator.email} within 14 days of paying and we'll refund it. A monthly renewal is not a new plan.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Charged by mistake</strong>, or charged twice: we refund it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>DMbot didn't work</strong> for a long time because of a problem on our side: ask us,
      and we'll look at each case. Write to {operator.email}.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Extra hours</strong> (the add-on hours you buy) can't be refunded, used or not.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    {paymentProvider} is the seller. If you are in the EU or the UK, it handles your legal
    right to withdraw, and your invoices and tax.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-to-ask">How to ask</h2>
  <p>
    Write to {operator.email} from the email on your account, and say what happened. We answer
    within 5 working days. Refunds are made by {paymentProvider} to the card or
    account you paid with, and can take a few days to show.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
